## 1. HOW IT WORKS

```text
================================================================================
1. HOW IT WORKS
================================================================================
The automation has four phases. All four ship as code in your repo; you only
have to wire up the accounts.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Phase                      What happens                           Triggered by                     Bitrise workflow
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. PR quality gate         Lint, security scan, unit tests,       Push to any branch except        primary
                           e2e typecheck. MR cannot merge         main/master, and every
                           until green.                           merge request.

2. Real-device release     Builds a Release APK/IPA, uploads      Push (merge) to main or          deploy-android /
   test                    to Sauce Labs, runs Appium e2e on      master.                          deploy-ios
                           a real device, publishes JUnit +
                           HTML + Sauce video link.

3. Notifications           Posts pass/fail + build link to a      End of deploy-* workflows.       (step inside deploy-*,
                           Microsoft Teams channel (or email).                                     opt-in)

4. Developer self-service  One-command onboarding, local          Developer runs it locally.       npm run bootstrap,
                           pre-flight of every CI gate.                                            npm run pipeline:local
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Design rules everyone follows:
* Tests find elements by accessibility ID only (~loginButton). No XPath, no text or index locators.
* No secrets in code. Secrets live in Bitrise Secrets (CI) or a gitignored local vault (your laptop).
* CI never calls an AI/LLM. AI help is used only in the IDE when writing tests; the pipeline is deterministic.
* Android builds use the Release variant for Sauce. A Debug build has no Metro server on a real device and crashes into the red error screen.
