## 6. WRITING TESTS

```text
================================================================================
6. WRITING TESTS
================================================================================

6.1 Rules (enforced in review; also in tests/conventions.md)
1. Locators: accessibility IDs only (~username, ~loginButton, ~accountBalance).
2. Structure: tests call page objects (LoginPage, DashboardPage); no raw driver.$() in test files.
3. Naming: describe('<Feature>'), it('<user> <action> and <expected outcome>').
4. Assertions: at least one expect(...).toBeDisplayed() on a visible outcome.
5. Waiting: no fixed sleeps; use waitForDisplayed / waitForExist inside page objects.
6. Secrets: read from process.env; never literal passwords.
7. Independence: every test starts from app launch.

6.2 What the framework gives you
Page objects extend BasePage from @enterprise/rn-appium-framework:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Helper                   Use it for
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
waitForId(id, timeout?)  Wait until ~id is displayed, return it
setValueById(id, text)   Wait, then type
tapById(id)              Wait, then tap. Hides Android soft keyboard first
exists(id)               True if ~id is in the tree (e.g. "still on login screen?")
diagnose(appPackage?)    When an element missing: lists on-screen IDs, checks foreground,
                         pulls native crash block from logcat into CI log
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example page object:
import { BasePage } from '@enterprise/rn-appium-framework';
export class LoginPage extends BasePage {
  async login(user: string, pass: string) {
    await this.setValueById('username', user);
    await this.setValueById('password', pass);
    await this.tapById('loginButton');
  }
}

6.3 Make your app testable
Give every element a test needs a stable accessibility ID:
// React Native
<TextInput accessibilityLabel="username" testID="username" />
<Pressable accessibilityLabel="loginButton" testID="loginButton" />
<Text accessibilityLabel="accountBalance" testID="accountBalance">{balance}</Text>
Native Android: android:contentDescription="loginButton".
Native iOS: accessibilityIdentifier = "loginButton".

6.4 Add a test
1. Add/extend a page object in tests/pages/ (extends BasePage) with new locators.
2. Add a test file under tests/<feature>/<name>.test.ts.
3. Run npm run test:e2e:verify (typecheck) and npm run pipeline:local.
4. Push and open an MR. The real-device run happens after merge.
Using AI in IDE (optional): paste prompt from prompts/reactnative-appium.prompt.md
with tests/conventions.md into Copilot/Cursor, then review draft.

6.5 Run on Sauce from your laptop (optional)
export TEST_TARGET=sauce
export SAUCE_USERNAME=$(scripts/vault-get.sh SAUCE_USERNAME)
export SAUCE_ACCESS_KEY=$(scripts/vault-get.sh SAUCE_ACCESS_KEY)
export TEST_PASSWORD=$(scripts/vault-get.sh TEST_PASSWORD)
export SAUCE_APP_URI=storage:filename=<your-app>.apk
npm run test:e2e
Local emulator: leave TEST_TARGET unset and set APP_PATH to your built .apk/.app.
```

