## 10. SECURITY RULES

```text
================================================================================
10. SECURITY RULES
================================================================================
* Never commit: .env, .vault/secrets.env, .provision.env, keystores, *.p12, provisioning profiles, or src/config/buildEnv.ts with real values (scripts/security-scan.sh checks before push).
* Secrets live in Bitrise Secrets (CI) and ERPM (humans). Local copies stay in gitignored files.
* API tokens used for provisioning get an expiry date and are revoked or deleted after setup.
* TEST_PASSWORD is the only secret exposed to PR builds; Sauce keys are not.
* Default branch is protected: no direct push, no force push; pipeline must pass.
* npm audit runs in report-only mode inside security scan; review high/critical findings each release.
* Teams Workflows URLs contain a sig= token: treat them as secrets. security-scan.sh fails the build if one is committed.
* If any secret leaks: rotate it first, then clean up history.
```

